===== ANDROID DEVELOPMENT WEEK 1 CHEATSHEET WITH QUESTIONS & ANSWERS =====

1. Android
- Open-source OS by Google based on Linux kernel
- Designed for touchscreen mobile devices (smartphones/tablets)
- Uses Java/Kotlin apps running on ART/Dalvik runtime

2. Android Studio
- Official IDE for Android app development
- Based on IntelliJ IDEA
- Provides code editor, debugger, emulator, build tools

3. Android SDK
- Software Development Kit containing APIs and tools to build Android apps

4. Android Project Structure

MyApp/
 ├─ app/
 │   ├─ src/
 │   │   ├─ main/
 │   │   │   ├─ java/           # Source code (Java/Kotlin)
 │   │   │   ├─ res/            # Resources (layouts, images, strings)
 │   │   │   ├─ AndroidManifest.xml  # App metadata & components
 │   │   │   └─ assets/          # Raw asset files
 │   ├─ build.gradle            # Module build config
 ├─ build.gradle                # Project build config
 ├─ settings.gradle             # Project settings

5. AndroidManifest.xml
- Declares app package name, components (Activities, Services, etc.)
- Defines permissions required by app
- Specifies app icon, label, theme
- Declares entry point Activity with MAIN and LAUNCHER intent filters

Example:
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    package="com.example.myapp">
  <application
      android:icon="@mipmap/ic_launcher"
      android:label="@string/app_name"
      android:theme="@style/AppTheme">
    <activity android:name=".MainActivity">
      <intent-filter>
        <action android:name="android.intent.action.MAIN" />
        <category android:name="android.intent.category.LAUNCHER" />
      </intent-filter>
    </activity>
  </application>
</manifest>

6. Activity
- Represents a single screen with user interface
- Hosts Views such as Button, TextView, EditText
- Manages its own lifecycle (onCreate, onStart, onResume, etc.)

7. Resources (res/)
- XML layouts (res/layout/)
- Drawable images (res/drawable/)
- String values (res/values/strings.xml)
- Colors, styles, themes (res/values/)

8. Gradle
- Build system used by Android Studio
- Manages compiling, dependencies, APK packaging
- Uses build.gradle files to configure builds

Example build.gradle snippet:
android {
    compileSdkVersion 33
    defaultConfig {
        applicationId "com.example.myapp"
        minSdkVersion 21
        targetSdkVersion 33
        versionCode 1
        versionName "1.0"
    }
}
d
dependencies {
    implementation 'androidx.appcompat:appcompat:1.5.1'
}

